// When defining the object, the caller provides a template structure for the
// object in a TPM2B_PUBLIC structure (inPublic), an initial value for the
// object’s authValue (inSensitive.userAuth), and, if the object is a symmetric
// object, an optional initial data value (inSensitive.data). The TPM shall
// validate the consistency of the attributes of inPublic according to the
// Creation rules in “TPMA_OBJECT” in TPM 2.0 Part 2.
//
// If fixedTPM is SET in the object’s parent, then fixedTPM shall equal
// fixedParent in template. If fixedTPM is CLEAR in the parent, this attribute
// shall also be CLEAR in template.
TpmTestVector(
  name: "[TPM2_Create] fixedTPM not consistent with parent",
  spec_versions: [
    184,
  ],
  test_sequence: [
  ]
)
